# A message delivered to a regular mailbox goes into all mail in the
# same injection, with its own uid there. Nothing is moved afterwards,
# and the flags need no copying, since a flag belongs to the message.
#
# The session here is on all mail, not on INBOX, so the EXISTS for an
# append to INBOX is itself the thing being tested.
depends allmail
send 8
e append INBOX () {171+}
From: =?utf-8?q?G=C3=B8ril?= <goril@example.com>
To: script@test.oryx.com
Subject: fresh
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Message-Id: <fresh@example.com>

hello
receive 4
* 21 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 22] next uid
e OK [APPENDUID 1 21] done
send 1
f fetch 21 (uid envelope)
receive 2
* 21 FETCH (UID 21 ENVELOPE ("Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200" "fresh" (("=?ISO-8859-1?q?G=F8ril?=" NIL "goril" "example.com")) NIL NIL ((NIL NIL "script" "test.oryx.com")) NIL NIL NIL "<fresh@example.com>"))
f OK done
end
